  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Ins 208.05 Prehearing Statements",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ins 208.05 Prehearing Statements.\n\n(a) At least 7 days before the prehearing conference, all parties shall file with the hearing clerk and serve on the other parties prehearing statements.\n\n(b) Prehearing statements shall include, by numbered paragraphs, a detailed, comprehensive, and good faith statement, setting forth the following:\n\n(1) Statement of the facts;\n\n(2) Disputed issues of fact;\n\n(3) Applicable law;\n\n(4) The rate the party believes is commercially reasonable;\n\n(5) A detailed description of the party’s methodology for calculating the rate;\n\n(6) A list of all exhibits to be offered in the direct case of each party;\n\n(7) A copy of each document or exhibit;\n\n(8) A list of all witnesses to be called at the hearing, together with a brief summary of their testimony; and\n\n(9) The status of settlement negotiations.\n\n(c) Except for good cause shown, only witnesses listed in the prehearing statement shall be allowed to testify and only exhibits, so listed, shall be received in evidence.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Ins 200) #13073-A, eff 7-27-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ins200.html"
}
